# Programme authority documents are copied in byte-identical from their approved
# sources and must never be reformatted — see docs/programme/README.md.
#
# They use Markdown hard line breaks (two trailing spaces) in their front-matter
# blocks, which `git diff --check` would otherwise report as whitespace errors.
# Disabling the whitespace check here keeps the documents verbatim (their SHA-256
# hashes are recorded in the readiness report) without weakening the check for
# actual source code.
docs/programme/*.md -whitespace
